abstract: >-
  Regime-Based World Modeling (RBWM) is a meta-epistemic architecture designed
  to map model validity across two orthogonal axes: the Regime Axis (R),
  representing emergent complexity levels, and the Epistemic Layer Axis (L),
  representing the derivation distance from raw observation to theoretical
  construct. The framework generalizes the Regime-Gating Principle, positing
  that a scientific claim is only epistemically valid if its primary variables
  are "driver-near" within the phenomenon's operative regime.
